# .trivyignore — unfixable CVEs suppressed from the gating Trivy scan.
#
# All entries below have been reviewed and are unfixable at this time.
# Each is documented in SECURITY.md with the rationale and a tracking reference.
#
# ── AL2023 packages: fix versions identified by Trivy but not yet in repo ────
# glibc: DoS via iconv() — fix: 2.34-231.amzn2023.0.4 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-4046

# cpython: incomplete control-char validation in http.cookies
# fix: python3 3.9.25-1.amzn2023.0.5
CVE-2026-3644

# cpython: arbitrary code execution via command injection in webbrowser.open()
# fix: python3 3.9.25-1.amzn2023.0.5
CVE-2026-4786

# cpython: arbitrary code execution/info disclosure via use-after-free in
# decompression — fix: python3 3.9.25-1.amzn2023.0.5
CVE-2026-6100

# openssh/openssh-clients: privilege escalation via scp legacy protocol
# fix: 8.7p1-8.amzn2023.0.17 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-35385

# urllib3 (pip): fix version not yet published on PyPI
# CVE-2026-44431: info disclosure via cross-origin redirects forwarding
#   sensitive headers
# CVE-2026-44432: DoS via excessive HTTP response decompression
# Both fixed in urllib3 2.7.0 per Trivy's advisory DB, but 2.7.0 does not
# exist on PyPI yet -- `pip3 install 'urllib3>=2.7.0'` fails outright
# (highest available is 2.6.3, the version already pinned here). Remove
# this suppression and bump the Dockerfile's urllib3 floor once 2.7.0 is
# published: https://pypi.org/project/urllib3/#history
CVE-2026-44431
CVE-2026-44432

